very on real dirty state remains observed-not-committed, no signed tag).\n- `tests/test_badf_git_shadow.py`: thresholds move to the new counts (≥7 / ≥15 / ≥21); the tamper test and every recomputation unchanged; still green in CI and in the composed world (the fixtures now carry `tests/`, #160).\n- `skills/badf-git/evidence/shadow-evidence.md`: measurement table refreshed; \"root stays `DESIGNED` for GIT-J\" → \"root `ACTIVE` at GIT-J (WP-0087, #169)\"; **seven → six subskills** here and in the GIT-I doctrine section of `GITHUB_CONTROL_PLANE.md`; the honest first sentence and the non-coverage list stay.\n- No registry, lifecycle, gate, compose or workflow change; own composition record + G07 self-dossier; reconciles the land-time-current WP.\n\n## Test list\n- existing `ShadowRecordTests` (8) green at the new thresholds; `test_tampered_shadow_record_is_refused` unchanged.\n- `test_shadow_evidence_doc_names_every_case_and_gap_and_root_is_active`: doc tokens now include \"ACTIVE\", \"six subskills\", \"#169\".\n\n## Out of scope\n- any change to the shadow's contract parts or the tools; a re-measure of the staleness/release cases on new heads (kept as the real cases they are).\n\n**Version tier:** patch (evidence + docs + test thresholds). **Lean mode:** advisory.\n\n🛑 Filed for the record; proceeds under the operator's standing \"complete the below\" directive after GIT-J lands (QA/REV by BARCHI-1 as for #160/#169).\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
